ok><name>AZEKAWA KAZUE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJITA MASAHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TUBOTA KENJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AZEKAWA, KAZUE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITA, MASAHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TUBOTA, KENJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A deodorant and antimicrobial water absorbent comprising a water absorbing resin (A), a compound (B) having an antimicrobial activity against ammonia-producing bacteria and a drug (C) having the ability to neutralize ammonia or to neutralize and adsorb it, with the components (A) and (B) being mixed with each other and/or bonded to each other; a process for the production thereof; and absorbent articles each having an absorbant layer comprising the water absorbent and a fibrous support holding the absorbent thereon. The water absorbent is excellent not only in deodorant and antimicrobial performances but also in absorption performance essential to an absorbent and handleabilities as powder (such as powder fluidity and resistance to blocking due to moisture absorption). The absorbent articles produced by using the absorbent can absorb liquids such as urine, blood and body fluid and exhibit deodorant and antimicrobial activities. The absorbent is useful for paper diapers for adults and children, pads for urinary incontinence, sanitary napkins, pantie liners, pads for breast milk, puerperal mats, medical underpads and so on.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce matériau, désodorisant et antimicrobien, absorbant l'eau comprend une résine absorbant l'eau (A), un composé (B) doté d'une action antimicrobienne et un produit (C) capable de neutraliser l'ammoniac ou de le neutraliser et de l'absorber, les constituants A et B étant mélangés ou liés l'un à l'autre. L'invention porte également sur la production de ce matériau ainsi que sur des articles absorbants pourvus d'une couche absorbante constituée du matériau absorbant l'eau et d'un support fibreux retenant ledit matériau. Ce matériau, aux qualités désodorisantes et antimicrobiennes remarquables, est également doté d'excellentes caractéristiques d'absorption, ce qui est essentiel pour un agent absorbant. Il est, de surcroît, très maniable sous forme de poudre (fluidité et résistance à toute obstruction due à l'absorption d'humidité). Les articles absorbants produits à l'aide de ce matériau, qui sont capables d'absorber des liquides tels que l'urine, le sang et les liquides organiques, ont une action désodorisante et antimicrobienne. Ce matériau absorbant convient à la fabrication de couches pour enfants et adultes, de coussinets contre l'incontinence urinaire, de serviettes hygiéniques, de garnitures pour collants, de compresses d'allaitement, de nappes puerpérales, de protège-draps à usage médical, etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreemen